    breaks the next time the deploy job runs, not at deploy time.
  - The existing [38;5;153mnotes[39m contents are not archived anywhere by this change. If you want a safety net before the deploy job
    picks 003 up, a [38;5;153mpg_dump[39m/[38;5;153mSELECT id, notes ... WHERE notes IS NOT NULL[39m snapshot beforehand is the cheap version.

  Also worth a check: SQLite only supports [38;5;153mDROP COLUMN[39m from 3.35 (2021). If the deploy target is older, this migration
  errors and the table-rebuild pattern is needed instead — I couldn't tell the engine version from the repo.

